This is a sample YODL document used to test the po4a YODL parser.

The tt(yodl) program reads one or more input files and writes one output
file.  Inline macros such as em(italic) stay inside the whole paragraph.

center(
    tt(yodl) em(flags) em(inputfile) em(\[inputfile...\])
)

itemization(
    it() tt(-D) em(name): Defines em(name) as a symbol.
    it() tt(-I) em(directory): Searches include files in a directory.
)

chapter(Using the yodl program)

Some text containing the verb(latex --output) macro, which is never translated.

nested(foo(bar baz), qux) ends this document with an escaped paren \(x\).
